findings.proposed_fix:
Owner decides:
(a) whether the blog's Organization/LocalBusiness should point identity to the main site, via url = business.url or sameAs += business.url (a template change once approved);
(b) whether to fix the about.me text (remove '10 năm kinh nghiệm' and 'student and web developer'; align districts) or drop it from sameAs and the footer;
(c) whether to align the brand name across GBP, main site and blog (business.yml display_name).
The safe part needs no decision: move the sameAs list into _data/navigation.yml (e.g. a `sameas: true` flag on the 'HỒ SƠ & MẠNG XÃ HỘI' links) and read it in seo.html, so the markup and footer cannot drift.

Phase 1 (SAFE_TEMPLATE, one file): in _includes/seo.html, replace the seo_title block at lines 3-12 with:

{%- assign seo_brand = business.brand | default: site.title -%}
{%- capture seo_long_suffix %} - {{ site.title }}{% endcapture -%}
{%- capture seo_hub_suffix %} - Cẩm nang {{ site.title }}{% endcapture -%}
{%- assign seo_title = page.seo_title | default: page.title -%}
{%- if page.url == '/' and page.meta_title -%}{%- assign seo_title = page.meta_title -%}
{%- elsif seo_title -%}{%- assign seo_title = seo_title | remove: seo_hub_suffix | remove: seo_long_suffix -%}{%- unless seo_title contains seo_brand -%}{%- assign seo_title = seo_title | append: ' | ' | append: seo_brand -%}{%- endunless -%}
{%- else -%}{%- assign seo_title = seo_brand -%}{%- endif -%}

What this does and does not touch:
- og:title and twitter:title already reuse seo_title, so they follow automatically.
- No front matter changes. H1s, breadcrumbs and BlogPosting.headline use page.title and stay the same.
- The homepage keeps its meta_title branch, so frozen-homepage.json and check-regressions H1 keep passing.
- business.brand already exists in _data/business.yml, so no new business data is introduced.

Verification:
1. Build locally.
2. Run check-regressions.py and expect 9/9.
3. Rerun audit_head_meta.py and analyze.py and expect: 0 titles ending in the long suffix, 7,046 ending in ' | Nguyễn Tú' (all non-home, non-stub pages), head term in 18 titles, 0 twice, 0 duplicates.
4. Diff the old and new _site and confirm that only <title>, og:title and twitter:title lines change.

Phase 2 (optional, separate engine PR): remove the hard-coded suffix strings from the 7 hub/chu-de .md titles, keeping the ' - ' separator that the H1 split relies on, and from generate-listing-pages.py lines 92 and 120. Add a check-regressions invariant: no non-home title contains ' - Thuê Xe Máy Hà Nội Nguyễn Tú', and no title contains the head term twice.

After deploy, monitor the one ranking URL (/du lịch/2026/09/19/thue-xe-may-quan-hoan-kiem-gan-pho-co/) for 'thuê xe máy phố cổ hà nội'. Search Console for the blog is still unavailable (SEO-109), so ranking impact can't be measured directly.

SAFE_TEMPLATE in /home/user/blog/_layouts/hub.html, inside the existing 'Chủ đề con' `{% if cnt > 0 %}<li>…` item, after the count span, add:
{% assign _cl = site.data.seo-leads[cid] %}{% if _cl and _cl.size > 0 %}<br><span class="hub-lead">Nên đọc trước: <a href="{{ _cl[0].u | relative_url }}">{{ _cl[0].t }}</a></span>{% endif %}
This needs no extra site.posts loop: O(children) lookups in existing data, and it follows lead changes from KW-02 automatically. Verify: build, check-built-links.py (0 broken), check-regressions.py 9/9, and diff showing only the 6 pillar pages changed.

verdicts.implementation_notes:
FILE: _includes/article-breadcrumb.html only. Tested variant: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-blog/c0138ac4-51ee-5beb-a1c9-21d2311d0295/scratchpad/audit/review-SD-01/variants/B-sd01only.html.

1) Directly after the line `{% assign bc_child_node = site.data.factory-taxonomy[bc_child_id] %}` and BEFORE the `{% capture bc_parent_url %}`, insert:
`{% if bc_parent == nil and bc_child_node %}{% assign bc_parent = site.data.factory-parents[bc_child_node.p] %}{% endif %}`
It must come before bc_parent_url and bc_child_url are captured, so the existing `{% if bc_parent and bc_child_node %}` builds /an-toan-phap-ly/<child.s>/. It runs only when the parent key is unknown, so every post whose parent_id already resolves is unchanged. All 56 taxonomy children have a valid p (verified).

2) Replace the 5 JSON-LD lines from position 3 through `{% endif %}` with:
```
{%- assign bc_pos = 3 -%}
{%- if bc_parent %}
{"@type": "ListItem", "position": {{ bc_pos }}, "name": {{ bc_parent.t | jsonify | replace: '</', '<\/' }}, "item": {{ bc_parent_url | absolute_url | jsonify | replace: '</', '<\/' }}},
{%- assign bc_pos = bc_pos | plus: 1 -%}
{%- if bc_child_node %}
{"@type": "ListItem", "position": {{ bc_pos }}, "name": {{ bc_child_node.t | jsonify | replace: '</', '<\/' }}, "item": {{ bc_child_url | absolute_url | jsonify | replace: '</', '<\/' }}},
{%- assign bc_pos = bc_pos | plus: 1 -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif %}
{"@type": "ListItem", "position": {{ bc_pos }}, "name": {{ page.title | jsonify | replace: '</', '<\/' }}, "item": {{ page.url | absolute_url | jsonify | replace: '</', '<\/' }}}
```
Keep the last name as page.title and keep the visible `page.title | split: ' - ' | first` unchanged in this change.

DO NOT include the auditor's bc_title / `remove: bc_suffix` hunk. It changes the visible label on 25 posts (e.g. 'Tuyến Hà Nội' becomes the full title) and is a separate finding. DO NOT change _layouts/post.html: the fallback there produces no output change. DO NOT edit _data/factory-parents.yml to add an alias: the file is generated by restore-foundation.py ('Không sửa tay') and generator-drift checks would flag it. DO NOT touch the 4 _posts files: they are PUBLISHED with QA evidence SHA.

Edge cases verified in the mini build:
- unknown parent and unknown child: 3 items (Home, Cẩm nang, title);
- alias parent with no child_id: 3 items;
- legacy post resolved through factory-map: unchanged;
- valid parent with unknown child (C-HD-NGUOI-MO, C-THUE-THUE-NGAY, 'undefined'): unchanged, 4 items;
- titles containing '</' or quotes: escaped and valid.
No impact on redirect stubs, which use meta refresh and not the post layout, or on hubs, pagination, 404 or the homepage, because the include is used only by post.html. Whitespace control `{%-` is supported by Liquid 4.0.4 (GitHub Pages).

Verify after the change:
- quality-gate full mode;
- re-run scripts/seo/check-regressions.py, scripts/factory/check-built-links.py and scripts/faq/faq_parity_check.py;
- re-run /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-blog/c0138ac4-51ee-5beb-a1c9-21d2311d0295/scratchpad/audit/review-SD-01/bc.py and expect null_name 0, no_item_nonlast 0, double_slash 0, len_mismatch 0;
- on the live site, check the 4 URLs in the Rich Results Test.

Optional separate engine commit: add a check to scripts/seo/check-regressions.py (new H-id) or check-built-links.py with these rules:
- positions run 1..n;
- every non-last ListItem has a non-empty name and a string item whose path has no '//' and resolves to a built route;
- the number of visible `nav.breadcrumb ol > li` equals the number of ListItems;
- names match only for non-last items, otherwise the 25 ' - ' titles fail.

Upstream (NEEDS_OWNER, not template): the factory-operator.py QA could also assert that front['parent_id'] == row['parent_id'], so aliases cannot be published again.

Rollback: git revert of the single include commit. Output returns to the current bytes.

